cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "tipping-early-warning"
abstract: >-
  Can a noisy time series warn us before a tipping point? A simulation study of
  early-warning signals (rolling variance and lag-1 autocorrelation) near the
  saddle-node bifurcation of the bistable model dx = (r + x - x^3) dt + sigma dW,
  with a control group and a sweep over noise level and ramp speed.
authors:
  - given-names: Fernando
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - dynamical systems
  - bifurcation
  - tipping points
  - early warning signals
  - critical slowing down
  - stochastic processes
